{{!--
  cargo-about template for THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt (#1081). Rendered by
  scripts/third_party_notices.sh, which appends sections 2-4; about.toml holds
  the configuration. Plain text, so every value uses triple braces: double
  braces would HTML-escape it.

  First-party MeteoCore crates are path dependencies, which have no `source`,
  and are left out of the lists. ds-bufr is one of them; the script appends
  its tinybufr licences in section 4.

  Lines starting with `@@` are instructions to the script, which removes
  them. `@@licence` starts a licence block, and the script drops a block that
  lists no crate, as one used only by first-party crates would. `@@crate`
  names a crate's source directory, where the script looks for the licences
  of bundled C libraries and for NOTICE files. `@@native` marks a crate that
  builds native code with `cc` or `cmake`, which the script must know.
--}}
